 "equipment_type": "Room sensor / operating unit",
 "applies_to": "Belimo 22RT...-5U00... room operating units with virtual or ePaper touch display, measuring temperature, humidity and CO2.",
 "summary": "The 22RT room operating unit is a wall sensor with a configurable display that measures room temperature and, depending on model, humidity and CO2. Over BACnet MS/TP it reports the measured values and lets the BMS read and write the temperature and ventilation setpoints, set the building operation mode, and control what the display shows (icons, buttons, CO2 traffic light). The occupant's local adjustments come back as the same setpoint objects.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "ROUS1 V2.2 / V3.0",
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Humidity, dew point and CO2 objects only apply to models with those sensors.",
  "MV 127 sets the bus unit of AI 1, AV 12 and AV 110; MV 100 only changes the display unit.",
  "MV 103 SetpointType uses state values 0 and 1 as printed in the document.",
  "Display objects (BV 110-125, MV 110-117) configure the screen layout and icons rather than the HVAC process."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Read AI 1 temperature (plus AI 2 humidity and AI 3 CO2 where fitted) and use AV 110 or the relative AV 111 as the zone setpoint, which the occupant can also change locally. Use MV 118 for comfort/eco/boost/off mode and AV 15 for the ventilation setpoint. Drive the heating/cooling and warning icons from the BMS if wanted.",
